.TH "LAGO" "1" "Sep 2026" "Lago CLI" "Lago CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
lago-order-forms-mark-as-signed - Mark an order form as signed


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlago order-forms mark-as-signed  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
This endpoint records the customer's signature on an order form, and creates the order that carries the quoted deal out.
Only a \fBgenerated\fR order form can be signed, so a \fB422\fR is returned once the order form has been signed, has expired or has been voided.
An \fBexecute_at\fR landing on or after the day the quoted deal stops being executable is rejected as well, so the order can never be scheduled past the term it bills.
A concurrent write on the same quote is reported as a \fB422\fR rather than retried, so a duplicated call can fail while the first one is still in flight.
This is a premium feature.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--execute-at\fP=""
	The date and time in UTC (ISO 8601) when Lago executes the order created from the order form. It must be in the future, requires 'execution_mode' to be set, and must fall strictly before the day the quoted deal stops being executable, otherwise signing is rejected with a '422'. When it is omitted, the order is created but not scheduled, and waits to be executed on demand.

.PP
\fB--execution-mode\fP=""
	How the order created from the order form is carried out. It becomes mandatory as soon as 'execute_at' is provided.; one of: execute_in_lago, order_only

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for mark-as-signed

.PP
\fB--idempotency-key\fP=""
	Idempotency key for safe mutation retries

.PP
\fB--input\fP=""
	Complete JSON request body or @file.json

.PP
\fB--signed-document\fP=""
	The document signed by the customer, as a base64 data URI ('data:;base64,\&'). Accepted content types are 'application/pdf', 'image/jpeg' and 'image/png', for a maximum of 10 MB. Once attached, it is exposed as 'signed_document_url' on the order form.


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	Override the Lago API key

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	Override the Lago API URL

.PP
\fB--confirm\fP=""
